  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(s\\) be the limiting sum of the geometric series \\(4-\\dfrac83+\\dfrac{16}{9}-\\cdots,\\) as the number of terms increases without bound. Then \\(s\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "a number between \\(0\\) and \\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2.4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2.5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3.6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "2.4"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The first term is \\(4\\) and the common ratio is \\(-\\frac{2}{3}.\\) Thus \\[ s=\\frac4{1-(-\\frac{2}{3})}=\\frac{12}{5}=2.4. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Find the ratio of the second term to the first",
        "Use \\(\\frac{a}{1-r}\\) because the ratio has absolute value less than \\(1\\)"
      ],
